{"t": 1794109622.5340066, "kind": "call", "tool": "github_create_pull_request", "args": {"base": "main", "body": "Fixes #57.\n\nThe API documents page numbers as 1-based (`?page=1` is the first page), but `catalog.pager.page()` computed the offset as `number * size`, so page 1 returned the second page (and page 0 returned the first).\n\nThis changes the offset to `(number - 1) * size` so `page(items, 1, size)` returns the first page.\n\nVerified locally: page 1 -> items[0:size], page 2 -> items[size:2*size], last partial page and out-of-range page behave as expected.", "head": "fix/pagination-57", "owner": "acme", "repo": "catalog", "title": "Fix page() to use 1-based page numbers (#57)"}, "ok": true}
